# [V2G20-2379] chain selection — three arms against everest-core main (ebcd36d)
# Evse15118D20, config-sil-dc-d20.yaml as shipped, two V2G roots installed.
# Station holds a valid chain under BOTH roots; evse_security handed the module chain B.
#
#   evse_security:E :: Requesting leaf certificate info: V2G
#   evse_security:E :: Found valid leaf: [".../client/cso/CPO_CERT_CHAIN_B.pem"]

### ARM-A: ask for root A (the one it also holds)  requestCAfile=ca/v2g/V2G_ROOT_CA.pem
--- chain the station served ---
 0 s:CN=SECCCert-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=CPO
   i:CN=CPOSubCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
 1 s:CN=CPOSubCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
   i:CN=V2GRootCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
--- handshake ---
New, TLSv1.3, Cipher is TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
Protocol: TLSv1.3
Verify return code: 20 (unable to get local issuer certificate)

### ARM-B: ask for root B                          requestCAfile=pki-rootb/V2G_ROOT_CA_B.pem
--- chain the station served ---
 0 s:CN=SECCCert-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=CPO
   i:CN=CPOSubCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
 1 s:CN=CPOSubCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
   i:CN=V2GRootCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
--- handshake ---
New, TLSv1.3, Cipher is TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
Protocol: TLSv1.3
Verify return code: 20 (unable to get local issuer certificate)

### ARM-C (control): send no certificate_authorities at all
--- chain the station served ---
 0 s:CN=SECCCert-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=CPO
   i:CN=CPOSubCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
 1 s:CN=CPOSubCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
   i:CN=V2GRootCA-B, O=EVerest, C=DE, DC=V2G
--- handshake ---
New, TLSv1.3, Cipher is TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
Protocol: TLSv1.3
Verify return code: 20 (unable to get local issuer certificate)

### the answer arm A should have had was available
$ openssl verify -CAfile ca/v2g/V2G_ROOT_CA.pem \
      -untrusted client/cso/CPO_CERT_CHAIN.pem client/cso/SECC_LEAF.pem
client/cso/SECC_LEAF.pem: OK
